2026-10-19 21:06 Implementation note (mcp-hub-worker).

What changed
- lib/MCP/Hub/Upstream/Http.pm: the resolved endpoint is checked against the
  configured url before it is stored. Scheme, host and port have to match --
  the default ports 80/443 are normalized, since Mojo::URL leaves an implicit
  port undefined. A relative endpoint ('/messages') is made absolute against
  the configured url first, so it matches by construction.
- A refused endpoint is never stored, so _sse_post has nothing to post to:
  the foreign origin receives no POST, and with it no configured header (the
  Authorization bearer among them).
- The refusal counts as a connect failure like any other: the connect fails
  with a clear reason ('SSE endpoint ... does not match the configured origin
  ...'), three of them within five seconds mark the upstream failed.
- The reason of the refused attempt is part of the error message, so
  'mcp-hub status' shows why the upstream failed and not only the count.
  This is a small addition to the existing message ('3 connect failures
  within 5s: <reason>'); the count alone was there before. Say the word if
  you would rather see the count only.
- POD of MCP::Hub::Upstream::Http states the rule.

Tests
- t/http.t: 'sse upstream: an endpoint on another origin is refused'. A fake
  SSE server announces the endpoint of a second server on another port: the
  connect fails with a reason naming the origin, the second server receives
  no POST, and the upstream ends up failed with the reason in the status row.
  The fake SSE server lives in the test file.

Verified
- prove -lr t/ green (16 files, 134 tests).
- Red against the old lib: t/http.t subtest 5 fails there -- the endpoint is
  trusted and the foreign origin receives the POST.

